prompt:
These are corporate environmental claims that our carbon-accounting rule set did not flag.
For each, identify any technical term, metric, or accounting concept that could hide a scoping or
boundary problem but is not covered by these nine existing rules: market-based vs location-based
Scope 2, REC/PPA grid matching, carbon neutral offsets, missing baseline year, missing scope
boundary, cherry-picked PUE, water accounting, future promises without milestones, matching
language.

CLAIMS:
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_026", "text": "In Asia Pacific, Alphabet's regional average Google CFE was 12%."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_027", "text": "In North America, Alphabet's regional average Google CFE was 70%."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_028", "text": "In Latin America, Alphabet's regional average Google CFE was 92%."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_041", "text": "In 2024, we diverted 85% of food waste from landfill through composting, donations, or other recovery efforts."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_043", "text": "The remaining 6% of plastic in packaging was hidden in places like box liners, seals, and adhesives."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_046", "text": "Flights rerouted to avoid creating contrails only used an average of 2% additional fuel, compared to control flights."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_048", "text": "The cost of reducing contrails through navigational avoidance could be in the range of $5–$25 per tCO2e."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_063", "text": "Google has achieved at least 80% CFE across nine out of 20 grid regions with Google-owned and -operated data centers."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_067", "text": "In 2024, combined scope 1 and scope 2 (market-based) emissions were 3.1 million tCO2e, representing a 241% increase compared to 2019."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_068", "text": "In 2024, scope 3 (ambition-based) emissions were 8.4 million tCO2e, representing a 25% increase compared to 2019."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_077", "text": "The community group hosts biannual events highlighting sustainability-related 20% opportunities."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_143", "text": "Google's climate target approach aligns with a 1.5°C scenario and utilizes the standard validation route for target setting."}
{"claim_id": "msft_sr_144", "text": "Microsoft decreased Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 29.9% from their 2020 baseline in FY24."}
{"claim_id": "msft_sr_145", "text": "Microsoft's Scope 3 emissions increased in FY24 by 26% from their 2020 baseline."}
{"claim_id": "msft_sr_151", "text": "The 17,000 metric ton CO2 reduction is comparable to avoiding the combustion of nearly 40,000 barrels of oil."}

Output ONLY a JSON array: [{"term": "...", "why_it_matters": "one sentence",
"example_claim_id": "..."}]. Return [] if nothing new.

